          "authorName": "@yagiyulle",
          "authorChannelUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/@yagiyulle",
          "isCreator": false,
          "text": "@h @helenbairaya7461 have seen many comments or videos from other Korean creators on various social media platforms. No matter if the procedure was successful or not, they mention multiple times they cannot publicly disclose which clinic they got their treatments from (if its sponsored, I am sure that is a different story). I am not fully familiar with their laws…. but it’s not a one time instance. I’m not sure if non-Korean influencers are told similar things when they film about the treatments or not. But just like how in Japan, you cannot film in a majority of places or how people’s faces are usually blurred when people film in public in most of Asia, I would say its just a matter of their laws being different🤷🏻‍♀️ (and it is likely related to their laws regarding defamation)",
