        {
          "commentId": "UgxUY13bMGevHwH2IcR4AaABAg.AKVy4jnftFiAcWQhjovjV6",
          "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LlAjOc8o3BM&lc=UgxUY13bMGevHwH2IcR4AaABAg.AKVy4jnftFiAcWQhjovjV6",
          "authorName": "@yagiyulle",
          "authorChannelUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/@yagiyulle",
          "isCreator": false,
          "text": "@GaryKoji-j3x  I agree in that it is a bit much, but I can also understand why the law is in place as well. Laws are going to be different in every country, and in Korea and other Asian countries, defamation laws are no joke (even if what you are talking about is true). \n\nI don’t know how accurate the translations are, but did a search on the internet. It seems like it the public sharing of information may pertain to the Medical Service Act, article 56 (it is long to summarize, but I would recommend looking it up if you are curious). I have seen many influencers say that if you dm them privately, they can share more information in a private chat. I doubt all are influencers are choosing to purposely gatekeep, but instead just following the laws. Tbh, I am personally uncertain if these laws pertains to foreigners who travel for medical tourism (would probably need to look at the forms before agreeing to services), but it seems to me everyone is being careful. \n\nThis is a whole separate matter, but a personal opinion I have is that people should not blindly follow an influencer’s recommendation and also do significant amount of research themselves before committing to any sort of procedure (invasive or not) to be fully aware of the risks.",
          "language": "latin(en etc)",
          "publishedAtText": "2주 전(수정됨)",
          "likeCount": 0
        },
        {
          "commentId": "UgxUY13bMGevHwH2IcR4AaABAg.AKVy4jnftFiAcbxfe6KFbw",
          "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LlAjOc8o3BM&lc=UgxUY13bMGevHwH2IcR4AaABAg.AKVy4jnftFiAcbxfe6KFbw",
          "authorName": "@nyumeria8657",
          "authorChannelUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/@nyumeria8657",
          "isCreator": false,
          "text": "@yagiyulle  as someone who works in the skin clinic industry, that is bs. You are allowed to name clinics - whether it is a sponsorship or not - but especially for negative feedback or comments/reviews, you place yourself at the risk of getting sued by clinics for \"defamation\" even if your review is legit and honest. Most of these influencers don't mention pricing cuz they have no idea how much the treatments cost because they are covered by the clinic as part of the collaboration in exchange for videos/content.",
          "language": "latin(en etc)",
          "publishedAtText": "13일 전",
          "likeCount": 0
        },
        {
          "commentId": "UgxUY13bMGevHwH2IcR4AaABAg.AKVy4jnftFiAcnbTzH8o0t",
          "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LlAjOc8o3BM&lc=UgxUY13bMGevHwH2IcR4AaABAg.AKVy4jnftFiAcnbTzH8o0t",
          "authorName": "@yagiyulle",
          "authorChannelUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/@yagiyulle",
          "isCreator": false,
          "text": "@nyumeria8657 Out of curiosity, do you work in the Korean skin clinic industry? I would be interested to hear more about this. The thing is, even before being an “influencer” and asking for skincare sponsorships became as widespread globally (I’m talking before or early 2010s), I remember watching Korean videos of people saying the same things. I did read some blog out of curiosity from people who got sponsorships, but it was made very clear that nothing was paid put of their pockets. \n\nI recognize that a lot of influencers nowadays get free treatments or discounts, but it wouldn’t make sense to get said free treatments without promoting the clinic right? This would just be a loss for the clinic. I would like to think international travellers have more freedom to discuss about these things compared to people that live in Korea presently, however, no one really talks about this topic in depth or discusses about the contracts or forms signed🤷🏻‍♀️.\n\nI am not pretty neutral about this topic, but as I mentioned, I just hope that everyone is making informed and well-thought out decisions when it comes to receiving any form of treatments as everything carries potential risks. Prices will vary based off of many different factors (ie foreigner “tax” being charged more than locals, skin condition, treatment recommendations, clinic location, promotions, interpreter services etc), and as not everyone will be getting exactly the same treatments, I personally don’t really see the need to disclose the exact amount you spent on services (a range might be helpful). To me, it makes more sense to direct the general public to contact the clinic directly to request for a quote🤷🏻‍♀️",
          "language": "latin(en etc)",
          "publishedAtText": "8일 전",
          "likeCount": 0
        }
      ]
    },
