          "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LlAjOc8o3BM&lc=UgxUv_j_T3_gmOw4p5F4AaABAg.ACNBvwyQIBwAN9cZQcOvnG",
          "authorName": "@homo_bighead",
          "authorChannelUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/@homo_bighead",
          "isCreator": false,
          "text": "there’s lotsss of different options and treatments that would definitely be better suited for your specific needs. procedures that would help build up your skin’s strength and elasticity instead. definitely just consult with a good professional and they’ll be able to direct you to a good treatment. but you also unfortunately have to be careful to not get talked into doing and paying for more than you need because some people take advantage of clients not knowing any better. not to talk poorly of aesthetics doctors and medical estheticians as a whole, i’m literally going to be a medical esthetician myself, but it doessss happen sometimes. i highly highly can’t recommend doing your own research enough. with so many treatments, things can get confusing and complicated with not knowing much about how the skin works and what all the different treatments mean and how they really affect your skin. so it’s definitely best to have a good idea of what exactly your needs are and what treatments you’re interested in, and then a professional can help direct you from there. but again, from what you’re saying i would definitely go for treatments that are designed to help rebuild your skin/dermis and help improve that thinning. :)",
          "language": "latin(en etc)",
